# Manifests

The package groups in `package-groups/` are the openSUSE Tumbleweed patterns of the same
name, carried over as Guix manifest files: the identifier and the summary
come from the pattern RPMs (`patterns-base-20241218`,
`patterns-server-20250313`), and the package list is that pattern's
requirements and recommendations with one operation applied — packages
that have no same-named Guix package are removed, and nothing is
substituted for them.

A group is kept only when its surviving packages still deliver what its
name promises.  Patterns dropped whole, with the reason:

- `basesystem` — an alias of `base`, by its own summary.
- `bootloader` — grub2, shim and mokutil have no same-named package; the
  bootloader is the installer's job here.
- `minimal_base` — branding, build-key, distribution-release and
  filesystem are distribution artifacts.
- `dhcp_dns_server` — kea has no same-named package, so the survivors
  would deliver DNS only under a name that promises DHCP too.

These files are plain Guix manifests: `guix package -m <file>` installs
the group on any Guix machine, with or without this installer.
